x-rec — NOTICE
=================

This repository is an independent, unofficial reimplementation of the method described in:

  X-Rec Technical Report
  ByteDance / TikTok-Data-Content Intelligence & TikTok-Data-Feed Quality
  arXiv:2609.29180v1, 24 Sep 2026
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.29180

Attribution and scope
---------------------
* The method, the algorithm and all reported production results belong to the paper's authors and
  ByteDance. Nothing in this repository is endorsed by, reviewed by, or affiliated with ByteDance,
  TikTok, or the paper's authors.
* This repository contains an implementation written from the paper's equations. Where the paper is
  silent or ambiguous, choices were made and are documented in xrec_ref/README.md.
* No code from ByteDance or TikTok is included here.

Third-party material
--------------------
* The paper PDF and its extracted text are NOT redistributed in this repository. Fetch them from arXiv
  under the terms of the arXiv license (http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/).
* No third-party datasets are bundled. The synthetic fixture in xrec_ref/data.py is generated at
  runtime.
* Referenced open-source projects (RQ-VAE-Recommender, RecBole, MiniOneRec, SASRec, ComiRec, DreamRec,
  LRURec, Latte, LLaDA-Rec, ContRec, MaskGR, DreamX-Rec, faiss) are listed by URL only and remain under
  their own licenses.

Numbers
-------
All numbers produced by this repository come from a synthetic fixture (6,000 items, 8 interest modes,
~1M parameters) or from a synthetic log written in MovieLens format by dataset.py. No real interaction
dataset is bundled, and no number here was measured on real user data. They are NOT comparable to the
paper's results on TikTok's streaming benchmark and must not be presented as a reproduction of them.
